From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:25:27 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/22] xlsx: write runs of shared trees as shared formulas

Consecutive cells down a column that hold shifted copies of one tree at the same offset from their
cells are written as one Excel shared formula: the first cell carries the text and `ref`, the
others only `si`. Written on their own, as before: copies that push a reference off the sheet,
array formulas (legacy, spilling or needing array evaluation), table headers, cell pictures, and
formulas Excel can't read as shared. Excel (observed: Microsoft 365) refuses to open a workbook
whose shared formulas hold a sheet-qualified reference such as `Lookup!$A$2:$B$21`, even to the
formula's own sheet; names and structured references are kept out as well.

Opening the result in Excel gives, for every cell, the same formula and the same recalculated value
as the per-cell file the previous build writes (checked on a 10 MB workbook with 432,120 formulas,
before and after a script of edits). Opening it with the previous build and saving again gives
the same per-cell formulas as saving the original.
